    <string name="guidance_title">Directions over music</string>
    <string name="guidance_like_baidu">Like Baidu</string>
    <string name="guidance_like_baidu_body">Directions go to the car on their own channel the moment they arrive and the car decides how the music sits under them, the way Baidu CarLife does it.</string>
    <string name="guidance_in_step">In step</string>
    <string name="guidance_in_step_body">FT mixes directions into the music and dips the music exactly while they speak. On drives where the car holds the music longer, directions wait for it.</string>
    <string name="guidance_on_time">On time</string>
    <string name="guidance_on_time_body">Directions speak the moment they arrive and FT dips the music with them, which on some drives reaches the car late.</string>
    <string name="quiet_title">Share sound without asking</string>
    <string name="quiet_on_body">FT passes other apps\' sound to the car by itself, with no question on the phone. To turn this off, run:</string>
    <string name="quiet_off_body">Android asks on the phone before FT can pass other apps\' sound to the car. Run this once from a computer with USB debugging on, and it stops asking:</string>
    <string name="picture_defaults_body">FT sends the car its own screen size, 1920×720 on a Corolla, with 3 Mbps of picture data. That is the most the Corolla has been tested with, and it kept up at 30 frames a second. FT starts at 20 frames a second and follows what the car asks for.</string>
    <string name="picture_changed_body">Changes take effect the next time the car connects.</string>
    <string name="picture_size_label">Size sent to the car</string>
    <string name="picture_size_car">Car\'s own</string>
    <string name="picture_size_baidu">Like Baidu</string>
    <string name="picture_size_custom">Custom</string>
    <string name="picture_width">Width</string>
    <string name="picture_height">Height</string>
    <string name="picture_fps_label">Frames a second</string>
    <string name="picture_rate_label">Picture data in Mbps</string>
    <string name="picture_rate_note">Baidu sends a Corolla 2.56. Anything above 3 is untested on the Corolla; if it is too much, the car asks for fewer frames a second.</string>
    <string name="picture_floor_label">Quality floor</string>
    <string name="picture_floor_note">Keeps every full picture small enough for the car to take, so the screen comes back after the car shows its own screens. Baidu does this on its newest phones. Lower numbers are sharper and bigger, Off sends whatever the phone makes.</string>
    <string name="picture_min_fps">Lowest frame rate to accept, 0 means no floor</string>
